DATA LICENSE (data/processed/ and obl/*.json)
=============================================

The CSV/JSON record files in data/processed/ and the derived OBL result
files in obl/ (gap_results.json, gap_interlevel.json,
item7_obl1_hint_strata_by_partner.json) are derivative records produced by
replaying publicly available Hanabi game logs through the engine in this
repository and computing the literal-information posterior at every play
action. They are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Use is permitted with attribution to (a) the paper referenced in README.md
and (b) the original sources of the underlying game logs:

- human_play_records.csv
    Source: hanab.live (https://hanab.live), accessed via the public API.
    The original game logs are user-submitted public replays. Usernames
    are pseudonymized (16-hex salted hashes; verified bot accounts keep
    their public names).

- agent_play_records.csv
    Source: HOAD (Hanabi Open Agent Dataset; Sarkar et al. 2023). HOAD
    re-implements rule-based agents from Walton-Rivers et al. (2017),
    Van den Bergh (2015), and Osawa (2015).

- human_ai_play_records.csv
    Source: HanabiData (Eger et al. 2017),
    https://github.com/yawgmoth/HanabiData. Original participant consent
    was obtained by Eger et al. as part of the original study.

- hint_records.csv, hai_game_participant_map.csv
    Derived from the same three sources above.

- llm_cg_records.json, llm_joint_posteriors.csv, llm_fallback_counts.json
    Source: LLM-vs-rule-based-AI Hanabi simulations generated for the
    paper (GPT-5.4 family via the OpenAI API; Qwen3.6-A3B via local
    inference).

- obl/gap_results.json, obl/gap_interlevel.json,
  obl/item7_obl1_hint_strata_by_partner.json
    Aggregate statistics computed from games generated by running the
    publicly released off-belief-learning checkpoints (Hu et al. 2021;
    https://github.com/facebookresearch/off-belief-learning). These
    aggregate results are facts about the generated games; the OBL code
    and checkpoints themselves are CC BY-NC 4.0 and are NOT redistributed
    here — see obl/NOTICE.

If you use these data, please cite the original sources above as well as
the paper.
